OL,3,GNEWSAThe ancient woodland left
OL,4,Auntouched for 100 years
OL,5,
OL,6,FIn a city with a population of almost
OL,7,F600,000 people, even if it prides
OL,8,Fitself on being one of the UK's
OL,9,Fgreenest, it is rare to find places
OL,10,Funtouched by human activity - but an
OL,11,Fancient woodland in Sheffield is home
OL,12,Fto just such an area, unofficially
OL,13,Fdubbed "No Man's Land", which has been
OL,14,Fleft to go wild for almost 100 years.
OL,16,FCovering 346 acres (1.4 sq km),
OL,17,FEcclesall Woods are to the south west
OL,18,Fof Sheffield, close to the border with
OL,19,Fthe Peak District, and they form the
OL,20,Flargest semi-natural woodland in South
OL,21,FYorkshire.
OL,23,APub: 12-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
