OL,3,GNEWSAThe ancient woodland left
OL,4,Auntouched for 100 years
OL,5,
OL,6,FNearly a century ago, 42 acres (17
OL,7,Fhectares) of the woods were fenced off
OL,8,Fand the area has been allowed to lie
OL,9,Fpretty much undisturbed by human
OL,10,Fvisitors ever since so flora and fauna
OL,11,Fcan flourish there.
OL,13,FBy contrast, according to a history
OL,14,Fcompiled by volunteer group Friends of
OL,15,FEcclesall Woods, whose members care for
OL,16,Fthe site in partnership with Sheffield
OL,17,FCity Council, the rest of the woodland
OL,18,Fhas seen a lot of activity, not only in
OL,19,Fthe last 100 years but even before.
OL,23,APub: 12-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
